sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Authenticated user
    participant API as UploadFileController
    participant Upload as UploadFileUseCase
    participant Storage as MinIO private quarantine
    participant Persistence as JPA persistence adapters
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Acceptance as JpaFileAcceptanceAdapter
    participant Relay as OutboxRabbitMqRelay
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ exchange / queues
    participant Listener as RabbitMqScanListener
    participant Scan as ScanFileUseCase
    participant AV as ClamAV clamd

    User->>API: POST /api/v1/files multipart file
    API->>API: Authenticate and validate HTTP boundary
    API->>Upload: upload(UploadFileCommand, InputStream)
    Note over API,Upload: The domain receives a command and stream, never MultipartFile.

    Upload->>Persistence: save StoredFile(UPLOADING)
    Persistence->>DB: INSERT file metadata with UPLOADING
    DB-->>Persistence: persisted
    Persistence-->>Upload: saved

    Upload->>Storage: store(fileId, measured stream)
    Note over Upload,Storage: Bytes are streamed to an opaque quarantine key. Size and SHA-256 are measured in flight.
    Storage-->>Upload: StorageReceipt(storageKey, storageVersion)
    Upload->>Storage: head(fileId)
    Storage-->>Upload: canonical size and version/ETag
    Upload->>Upload: Verify complete stream, declared size, stored size and version
    Upload->>Upload: completeUpload(...) -> PENDING_SCAN

    Upload->>Acceptance: accept(PENDING_SCAN, FILE_SCAN_REQUESTED)
    Acceptance->>DB: Save file metadata and Outbox event in one transaction
    Note over Acceptance,DB: FILE_SCAN_REQUESTED contains metadata only: id, size, SHA-256, storage key and version.
    DB-->>Acceptance: transaction committed
    Acceptance-->>Upload: accepted
    Upload-->>API: UploadFileResult(PENDING_SCAN)
    API-->>User: 202 Accepted with metadata only

    Note over Relay,MQ: The upload use case does not publish directly to RabbitMQ.
    loop Scheduled Outbox relay
        Relay->>DB: Find unpublished Outbox events
        DB-->>Relay: FILE_SCAN_REQUESTED event
        Relay->>MQ: Publish RabbitMqScanMessage
        MQ-->>Relay: Publisher confirm
        alt Broker confirmation succeeds
            Relay->>DB: Mark Outbox event as published
        else Confirmation fails or times out
            Relay->>Relay: Keep event unpublished for a later attempt
        end
    end

    MQ-->>Listener: Deliver message from scan queue
    Listener->>Scan: scan(ScanFileCommand with expected metadata)
    Scan->>Persistence: claimPendingScan(fileId, lease)
    Persistence->>DB: Conditional PENDING_SCAN -> SCANNING with lease
    alt Claim is not available
        DB-->>Persistence: No row updated
        Persistence-->>Scan: Empty claim
        Scan->>Persistence: findById(fileId)
        Persistence->>DB: Read current status
        DB-->>Persistence: Current status
        Persistence-->>Scan: Unclaimed result
        Scan-->>Listener: Current status
    else Claim succeeds
        DB-->>Persistence: SCANNING with lease
        Persistence-->>Scan: Claimed file
        Scan->>Scan: Verify message metadata against stored metadata
        Scan->>Storage: head(fileId)
        Storage-->>Scan: size and storage version
        Scan->>Storage: openStream(fileId)
        Storage-->>Scan: Private content stream
        Scan->>AV: INSTREAM chunks
        AV-->>Scan: OK, FOUND, invalid response or I/O error

        alt Explicit clean verdict
            Scan->>Persistence: completeScan(CLEAN, ScanAttempt)
        else Threat detected
            Scan->>Persistence: completeScan(INFECTED, ScanAttempt)
        else Retryable failure before attempt limit
            Scan->>Persistence: completeScan(PENDING_SCAN, ScanAttempt)
        else Terminal failure or attempts exhausted
            Scan->>Persistence: completeScan(SCAN_FAILED, ScanAttempt)
        end
        Persistence->>DB: Persist status, lease release and scan attempt
        DB-->>Persistence: committed
        Persistence-->>Scan: Completed status
        Scan-->>Listener: ScanFileResult(status)
    end

    alt CLEAN, INFECTED or SCAN_FAILED
        Listener->>MQ: basicAck after persistence
    else PENDING_SCAN
        Listener->>MQ: basicNack(requeue=false)
        MQ-->>MQ: Dead-letter to retry queue, TTL, then route back to scan queue
    else SCANNING result / expired lease path
        Listener->>Scan: recoverExpiredScan(fileId)
        Scan->>Persistence: recover SCANNING lease to PENDING_SCAN
        Persistence->>DB: Conditional lease recovery
        Listener->>MQ: basicNack(requeue=false)
    end

    Note over Upload,DB: UPLOADING is never accepted, scanned or downloadable. A complete upload must reach PENDING_SCAN before FILE_SCAN_REQUESTED.
    Note over Storage,DB: File bytes stay in MinIO. PostgreSQL stores metadata, status, attempts and Outbox events, not content bytes.
    Note over Scan,AV: Unknown antivirus responses, storage inconsistencies and scanner failures fail closed; only an explicit clean result can produce CLEAN.
    Note over User,API: Download is outside this use case: only CLEAN plus owner authorization permits content streaming.
